rified": false}, "website": {"url": "https://t.co/4nmwnih07V"}}}}, "edit_control": {"edit_tweet_ids": ["2082839964472185078"], "editable_until_msecs": "1785426319000", "edits_remaining": "5", "is_edit_eligible": true}, "grok_analysis_button": true, "grok_annotations": {"is_image_editable_by_grok": false}, "grok_translated_post_with_availability": {"data": {"associated_data": {}, "destination_language": "en", "entities": {"hashtags": [{"indices": [923, 930], "text": "Jepang"}, {"indices": [931, 938], "text": "Global"}], "symbols": [], "urls": [], "user_mentions": []}, "preview_translation": "CEO of AEON Co., Ltd., Akio Yoshida, expressed an apology after the second floor of Aeon Mall in Kashima City, Kumamoto Prefecture, collapsed due to a powerful earthquake that struck southern Japan on Tuesday (July 28, 2026).\n\nThe building collapse was accompanied by an explosion", "source_language": "in", "translation": "CEO of AEON Co., Ltd., Akio Yoshida, expressed an apology after the second floor of Aeon Mall in Kashima City, Kumamoto Prefecture, collapsed due to a powerful earthquake that struck southern Japan on Tuesday (July 28, 2026).\n\nThe building collapse was accompanied by an explosion believed to have been triggered by a gas leak, which killed three people.\n\n\"I feel deeply responsible. I extend my deepest condolences to the deceased victims and sincerely apologize to their families,\" said Akio Yoshida on Wednesday (July 29, 2026).\n\nRescue teams are still searching for victims in the rubble of Aeon Mall Kashima. Meanwhile, the cause of the explosion at the shopping center is still under investigation by local authorities.\n\nAs of Thursday (July 30, 2026), the death toll from the Kumamoto earthquake has risen to 34 people, with around 9,000 residents evacuated to evacuation centers.\n\nSource: Associated Press, BBC\n\n~R #Jepang #Global"}, "is_available": true}, "is_translatable": true, "legacy": {"bookmark_count": 9, "bookmarked": false, "conversation_id_st